<title>GERMANY: EMI chief says EMU delay could wreck project.</title>
<headline>EMI chief says EMU delay could wreck project.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Institute (EMI) President Alexandre Lamfalussy said on Tuesday that he was opposed to delaying the launch of European monetary union because such a move would entail considerable risks and could &quot;wreck&quot; the entire process.</p>
<p>Lamfalussy also noted that the European Union was on a &quot;fundamental convergence track&quot; and that the progress on covergence made so far made monetary union a realistic objective.</p>
<p>Lamfalussy was speaking at a news conference to mark the launch of the European Central Bank forerunner's third annual report.</p>
<p>He also said that monetary union was not likely to go ahead without Germany.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
